		 <td>                            
	                                   

<P>&#9;There were things to see, things to do. Important things. No idea what they were…but they were important.</P><br><P>&#9;I went to Qeynos that day, loaded heavy with skins. Lacking sleep, I stayed the night at Fish’s and set out the next morning to sell my skins. For the first time in a long time, the press and the sound of the streets of Qeynos felt good to me. There was something happening to me. I felt very alive. </P><br><P>&#9;Having reprovisioned mysef, I set out at dusk for my camp again, but not without first stopping by Voleen’s Bakery and purchasing a few fresh pies for Gnasher, as well as some coffee and tobbacco. It felt good to do. I knew from talking with him that Gnasher had a taste for sweets, and I had never done my strange gnoll friend the honor of a gift before. Considering the change that his words seem to have wrought in me over the last days, I concluded that it was appropriate.</P><br><P>&#9;After a forced march back to my camp and a quick nap, I struck out with my pack for Gnasher’s cabin. I shortly found him out back, futzing with the brewbarrel.</P><br><P>&#9;We stoked the fire in the hearth and boiled water for coffee. I rolled us both some cigarettes (I had not had the money to afford the new, pre-rolled tobbacco sticks that were becoming high fashion for the Qeynos elite)</P><br><P>&#9;We cut the pie and drank the coffee (Gnasher scalded his tongue, but enjoyed the novelty of fresh coffee immensely). </P><br><P>&#9;Over breakfast I told him the story of that night over two years ago, of the monster that took the form of Hager Sureshot. I told him of its last word to me…</P><br><P>&#9;…Delicious…</P><br><P>&#9;He sat for a long moment, the smoke from his cigarette rising in lazy circles to the ceiling, staring his yellow-eyed stare at some invisible point in the distance.</P><br><P>&#9;"Dangerrouz thing this monsterr iz. Change shape, change voice…and lovez pain and fearr, it doez. Strong too—to thrrow you off that high place. You arre big for a human."</P><br><P>&#9;I took a drag off my cigarette, letting the buzz from the tobbacco calm the edginess that had suddenly risen in me. "Have you ever heard of such a monster?" </P><br><P>&#9;Gnasher stared through the smoke into the distance, as though thinking far back into his past. "Only in bad dreamz…"</P><br><P>&#9;We drank our coffee in silence for a moment, Gnasher lapping especially quietly from his cup, and making only a minimal mess.</P><br><P>&#9;"I have to kill it." I announced. "I even kept the arrow. Although, at the time I didn’t know why. I have to kill it or I can never be truly at peace."</P><br><P>&#9;"You, kill it, pup? How will you find it?</P>         <br>
